{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And you shall serve YHWH your Elohim, and He will bless your bread, etc.</b> The intention of this verse is that most idolaters acknowledge and know that the honored Name — He is Elohei ha-Elohim and Adonei ha-Adonim (God of gods and Lord of lords), and their intention in idolatry is not [directed] toward it, but rather they think that through those worship-services there will be success for them. For example, they would worship the sun because they found it has dominion over the crops, and the moon over the springs and all the deep waters, and similarly with the rest of the host of heaven. How much more so would they think that there would be added good for them in the worship of the angels, because they are honoring the ministers of the great El. Therefore this verse says that through the worship of HaKadosh Baruch Hu alone will there be success and protection for them, and the uprooting of idolatry will not cause harm but will rather add good and blessing for you, for HaKadosh Baruch Hu will bless your bread — and this is a general principle for every food that is eaten — and He will bless your water, which is the father of every beverage that is drunk, and the blessing is an addition in them, that there shall be from them for you in very great abundance." "And He said, <b>and I will remove sickness from your midst</b> — meaning that I will remove sickness from within them, so that the foods and the beverages will be good and healthy; they will not produce illness but will heal from it. And He further said that there shall not be among them a woman who miscarries in the womb miscarrying, nor a barren woman in the womb and dry breasts, for when the foods and the beverages and the air are blessed, the bodies will be healthy, and the organs of seed will be fit to perform their function properly. And He mentioned the females, because miscarriage and barrenness are found in them more than in the males. And it is possible that the males are included in <b>and I will remove sickness from your midst</b>, for barrenness is a disease in the bodies, and regarding the men He speaks from the general, and afterward He mentioned the women, as He said, there shall not be among you barren male or barren female (Deuteronomy 7:14). And the reason for <b>in your land</b> is to include also the livestock, as He said there, \"and in your livestock.\" And He said, <b>the number of your days I will fulfill</b> — that he will not die in war or in a plague through change of the air, but rather in old age, so that he will fulfill days according to the number that is the life of man in his generations, such as seventy or eighty years, like the generation of King David. And I have already mentioned (Genesis 17:1 and above, 6:3) that all of these are miracles that HaShem performs in heaven and on earth, wonders for those who do His will.<br>And He said that just as He performs with them a sign for good, so He does to their enemies for evil — that He gives them a trembling heart and terror from the chambers, and furthermore He sends against them <b>the tzir'ah</b>, and it is a known species, like the bee, and the Sages mention it frequently: honey of bees, honey of tzir'in (Makhshirin 6:4, Bekhorot 7a). And the matter is that He sends this plague into the air of their land, like the locust that He sent in Egypt, and the yelek, the chasil, and the gazam — the great host that came in the days of Joel (Joel 2:25).<br>And the reason for <b>and it shall drive them out</b> is that it is a cause among them to be driven from the land, for it covers the eye of the land and darkens it, and they are unable to come to battle, and furthermore, it eats all the produce of the field, as it says in the curses, \"You shall bring out much seed to the field but gather little, for the locust shall consume it\" (Deuteronomy 28:38), \"All your trees and the fruit of your land the tzeltzel shall inherit\" (ibid. 42) — so too He says here that He does to our enemies. And the verse mentioned <b>the Hivite and the Canaanite and the Hittite</b> by way of brevity, and the intention includes all those mentioned above. And the correct view in my eyes is that these three — the majority of them did not go out to battle and did not fall by the sword, but were fortified in the strongholds, so He sent against them only this death, as it says concerning Egypt (Exodus 10:6), \"and they shall fill your houses and the houses of all your servants and the houses of all Egypt,\" and this is what He says in Mishneh Torah (Deuteronomy 7:20), \"and also the tzir'ah HaShem your Elohim will send among them until the remaining ones and the hidden ones perish from before you.\" And this tzir'ah crossed the Jordan with Joshua, and so they reported in tractate Sotah (36a). And they said (in Tanḥuma here) that it carried venom among them and killed them with it. And the truth is that even today it has harmful and deadly venom.<br>And it is written in Joshua (Joshua 24:11–12): \"And you crossed the Jordan and came to Jericho, and the men of Jericho fought against you — the Amorite and the Perizzite and the Canaanite and the Hittite and the Girgashite, the Hivite and the Jebusite — and I gave them into your hand,\" and it is written, \"and I sent the tzir'ah before you and it drove them out from before you — the two kings of the Amorite — not by your sword and not by your bow\" (Joshua 24:11–12). And the meaning of \"and it drove them out\" — the ones remaining among them — is that after I gave into your hand all those mentioned, I sent the tzir'ah to drive out the remaining ones and the hidden ones. And He said, \"the two kings of the Amorite,\" and they are Sihon and Og, whom He mentioned at the beginning (ibid. v. 8), and \"not by your sword and not by your bow did you do all these.\" And R. Abraham [Ibn Ezra] said (on Exodus 23:28) that the tzir'ah is a disease of the body derived from the root of tzara'at. And there is no need [for this]. And the reason for <b>and you shall serve YHWH your Elohim</b> is to render the service void for the unique Name (Sanhedrin 60a). And He said, <b>and He will bless</b>, <b>and I will remove</b>, in the manner of \"for I am YHWH your healer\" (Exodus 15:26). And I have already explained it, and the enlightened will understand it from there."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :register {:flags {0 ["God" "Lord"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:15:45.071067473Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}